e,"messageTitle":"Close the GUI window on the bye command","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":2,"deletions":1},"java":{"insertions":58,"deletions":7}}},{"hash":"552aa2278a9aff6962301df0608b8179777a25d1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Keep long task descriptions beside the status box","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":52,"deletions":9}}},{"hash":"4a52c12c72e492ec36c4ba3e9ee9047f6f408f46","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-Level-10\u0027","messageBody":"","tags":["Level-10"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"b2bd11b1388c1df69f422ca4c1032c5b183af713","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use varargs for Ui.showMessage","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":41,"deletions":38}}},{"hash":"8a5b7de9f1bc28b00c86dcb6b50905e0a96dd8bf","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-A-Varargs\u0027","messageBody":"","tags":["v0.2","A-Varargs"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-09-11T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"1ac1ab6a9298051a8f08c5ef0ca15b222a1c2bf2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add assertions for internal invariants","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":6,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":32,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"98edca9c6da99af411514b7df772973af1caabf1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Extract file-reading out of Storage.load","messageBody":"load() was 57 lines and mixed several unrelated concerns at one\nlevel: deciding whether the save file is even readable, handling\nthree different I/O failure modes, stripping a byte-order mark, and\nparsing/counting lines. That made it hard to see the actual loading\nlogic among the setup code.\n\nSplit it along those lines (SE-EDU code quality guidelines: avoid\nlong methods, keep each method at a single level of abstraction):\n\n- readLines() now owns every \"can this file be read at all\" case\n  (missing, not a regular file, wrong encoding, other I/O error) and\n  always returns a list, so load() no longer needs to branch on how\n  reading failed.\n- stripLeadingBom() isolates the one line of BOM-specific logic.\n\nload() itself now reads as a single story: get the lines, parse each\none, report how many were skipped. Behaviour is unchanged; verified\nwith `./gradlew check` (126 tests, Checkstyle clean).\n","tags":["A-FullCommitMessage"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":54,"deletions":33}}},{"hash":"323702e1349caacec4f41eed93199021ebb509e9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Split task-type dispatch out of Storage.parseTask","messageBody":"parseTask() read the common envelope fields (type tag, done flag,\ndescription) and then, in the same method, decided which concrete\nTask subclass to build from them. Those are two different levels of\nabstraction: \"read a saved line\" and \"which task type is this\",\nmixed together in one 38-line method (SE-EDU code quality\nguidelines: avoid long methods, single level of abstraction).\n\nbuildTask() now owns the type -\u003e constructor switch on its own,\ntaking the already-split fields. parseTask() reads as: split the\nline, read the done flag, build the task, apply the done flag.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged; verified with `./gradlew check` (126 tests,\nCheckstyle clean).\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":25,"deletions":14}}},{"hash":"dfa6114a35ce62d7700de42a1c78e4cf3b26ec62","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use streams for mapping and filtering tasks","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":12,"deletions":13}}},{"hash":"e7c327f04c0e092a5c75b3413e95de1921e23435","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #1 from Gnanes99/branch-A-Assertions","messageBody":"A-Assertions","tags":["A-Assertions"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"0ea950cc7deb0cd6359f25bdec7666e34057f3a5","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027